extraction_notes: "WB9 South America 2 printed 52-55 (cache p052-p055, page_offset 0); the people are introduced on 52-54 and the R.C.C. block runs 54-55. Printed 55 checked against a 110 dpi render, which agreed with the OCR on every number (P.P.E. 2D4+4, I.S.P. 2D6x10 + M.E. + 3D6/level, the skill bonuses). No pucara-red-giant class was in production on 2026-09-25. || XP: the Fallam, Ojahee and Pucara Red Giant ladder on printed 192, read off a render; lower bounds 0 / 2,201 / 4,401 / 8,901 / 18,001 / 26,001 / 36,001 / 52,001 / 76,001 / 100,001 / 150,001 / 200,001 / 275,001 / 350,001 / 425,001. The book prints a ladder for the race and the R.C.C. is played on its own, so it is stored. || ATTRIBUTES as printed (54; the OCR reads 1.Q. and semicolons for colons): I.Q. 3D4+8, M.E. 3D4+12, M.A. 3D6, P.S. 4D6+24 (supernatural), P.P. 3D6, P.E. 3D6+10, P.B. 2D6, Spd 2D4x10. || POOLS: M.D.C. 1D6x100 + P.E., +10 per level; P.P.E. 2D4+4; Horror Factor 11. mdc_base is stated, so no men_of_arms line. || BONUSES: +4 save vs magic and +5 vs horror factor stored. Immunity to mind control and possession is total and stays a natural ability rather than a save bonus. The stone missiles'' +3 to strike is conditional and is prose. || PSIONICS: master psionic; two powers each from Sensitive, Physical and Healing at level one as three starting groups, then one more from any of those three per level (powers_per_level 1 under categories_allowed). No Super category: the book says the stone powers take the place of super-psionics. The three stone powers are class abilities with their I.S.P. costs, not catalog powers (the survey''s decision). || SKILLS: Language and literacy: Pucara (98%) is Language: Native Tongue 98 plus Literacy: Native Language 98, both fixed; the catalog has no Pucara language row and none was stubbed. Language one of choice +15 as one Language: Other pick. Basic math is Mathematics: Basic 45+15; Climbing 40+10; Detect Concealment 25+10. W.P. Blunt, W.P. Sword and two of choice. Hand to Hand: Expert changes to Martial Arts or Assassin for one other skill each; the book states no alignment condition, so none is stored. || RELATED: the book prints R.C.C. Related Skills for a race played on its own, so they are granted: eight, plus one at levels 3, 5, 7, 10, 12 and 14. Communications Radio: Basic only; Domestic +10; Espionage Wilderness Survival, Tracking (people) and Detect Ambush through the Espionage entry, and Camouflage - which the catalog files under Military - as a Military entry narrowed to Camouflage only, because Military is otherwise None and the Espionage line alone would leave it unreachable; Mechanical any; Medical Holistic Medicine only; Physical any except Acrobatics; Rogue +2 except Computer Hacking; Technical +10; Wilderness +5; Pilot, Pilot Related, Science and W.P. any; Electrical none. Secondary: six, same limits without the bonuses. || EQUIPMENT: the book prints no Standard Equipment line; its Weapons and Body Armor lines are stored as a choice of the giant stone axe or hammer and a choice of stone plate or half plate (catalog rows pucara-stone-axe, pucara-stone-hammer, pucara-stone-plate-armor, pucara-stone-half-plate). The 40% chance of one captured energy weapon with 1D4 spare E-clips is prose. || MONEY: none printed; starting_money not stored."
