## Lore

The Pucara, called the Red Giants or the Red People, are scarlet-skinned giants
of the Andes. Most people take them for D-bee monsters that came through the
rifts, but the Nazca know otherwise: the giants are natives of Earth whose
civilization held the mountains long before humans reached South America.
Every Pucara is a master psychic able to make stone flow like wax.

Their small kingdoms feuded among themselves until humans spread and the Nazca
mastered line magic. Driven by greed and fear, the Pucara chose a warlike High
King and marched on the lowlands, massacring as they went. The Nazca answered
with rune warriors and line magic, broke the giant host, and hunted the
survivors for twenty years. The last of the Pucara burrowed deep into a
mountain and sealed themselves away, leaving the Nazca believing them
destroyed.

The Great Cataclysm cracked their hidden refuge open. Many giants now raid
humans, the Incas above all, from hidden peaks, and they strike Arkhons, the
Megaversal Legion and the Silver River nations too. Others stay underground and
want only to be left alone, and a few live on the surface and try, mostly in
vain, to befriend other peoples. All are raised for war, and war bands of 3D4
giants often travel with a mind mage or two.

## GM Notes

The Pucara population is about 200,000, scattered among dozens of mountain
kingdoms. Hostile Pucara slaughter anyone who befriends humans, but have so far
left most D-bee tribes alone and might someday seek allies, especially other
giants.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'pucara-red-giant');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'pucara-red-giant';

